    "created_at": "2016-11-16T13:20:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-11-16T13:20:43Z",
    "body": "> Should we then not require it to be empty?\n\nI think there a lot of existing documents that have non-empty `iframe` elements, so if we were to require `iframe` to be empty, the checker would start reporting errors for all those.\n\nBut maybe that is actually what we want at this point. Maybe we could change the spec to require it to be non-empty, and I could implement it that way in the checker, and monitor the feedback on it and that doesn’t result in a lot of pushback from authors (bug reports, general complaints), great.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
