    "created_at": "2016-11-16T14:04:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-11-16T14:04:28Z",
    "body": "> 709 out of 165,162 pages (~0.4%). Of these, 422 have an `<a href>`, 94 have a `<script>`.\n\nThanks!\n\nSo ~0.4% usage seems like a low enough number that it’d be appropriate to change the spec to say that `iframe` must be empty in HTML just as the spec says it must be in the XML syntax.\n\nShould I go ahead and update this PR to make it say that?\n\n(I realize ~0.4% usage would be way to high if what we were talking about here is removing from a spec a feature that has UA requirements—and way too high for browsers to be able to drop the feature. But this change would have no impact on UA requirements, so in that light I think ~0.4% usage is low enough to not cause unacceptable disruption/frustration for authors.)\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/260954219/reactions",
